      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "Claude Opus 5",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-25T12:30:00Z",
      "note": "The anchor is the attacker’s exploit-contract creation whose constructor calls GiddyVaultV3.compound() at 0x5f0ad32c00641d1d2bb628ff341e0d4bb4494318 with an operator signature and three SwapInfo entries naming aggregator 0x7326a1ab0d696ae317958d136d6e4c693ea34528 and attacker-chosen tokens; it is the earliest transaction the attacker EOA sent against Giddy. The vault is not upgradeable: identical runtime code hash at the deployment block 24923987 and at block 24942491 with a zero EIP-1967 slot, so the exploited code is 2.58 days old, deployed by 0x16bcac66daa7c866192512a0eb157bb0486e3183, which is not an attacker address. The loss is traced end to end: the three g-share balances credited in the anchor are redeemed one for one into yb-tBTC, yb-cbBTC and yb-WBTC and then unwrapped into 3.435705122670142444 tBTC, 6.70925926 cbBTC and 6.04749743 WBTC, which is what the components record."
    }
